  (text "D501: Schottky diode, SW to VOUT -- AP3031 has no internal Schottky/VOUT pin (unlike\nAP3036B), so pin1 (SW)'s own datasheet text 'Connect external inductor and Schottky'\nrequires this external diode. B5819W (LCSC C64885, SOD-123, 40V/1.5A, Vf 600mV@1A --\ncomfortably above the panel's ~9V/40mA operating point in both reverse-voltage margin\nand forward current) picked from JLCPCB's in-stock Schottky diode listing (525,050\nunits live 2026-11-15 via jlcpcb-search MCP); verified against its own LCSC spec sheet,\nnot assumed. Anode ties to the SW/L501 node, cathode ties to the VOUT node (same node\nas C502, LED_A and U501 pin5/OV -- OV needs no separate wire since it already shares\nthis pin slot/net with VOUT, see the Backlight driver note below)." (at 20 540 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid f49c7b23-1e3a-4b8a-9c21-7d5e8a2c6f10)
  )
