  (text "4-wire SPI mode strap: IM0=GND, IM1=+3V3, IM2=+3V3 (pins 36/37/38)" (at 227.38 192.63 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid fd579777-85c2-47f6-9424-51d3b0359641)
  )
  (text "Display subsystem (pilink-7el.5) -- Crystalfontz CFAF240320A0-024SN, 240x320 native\n(rotated 90deg to 320x240 in firmware via ST7789V MADCTL/MV), 4-wire SPI.\nJ501 pin table sourced directly from Crystalfontz's own datasheet (Rev 1v2, 2021-03-26),\nsection 6, SPI-mode column (4-wire SPI selected via IM0=0/IM1=1/IM2=1). SDO (pin 4) and\nTE (pin 5) are marked no-connect per the datasheet (write-only use, no tearing-effect\nsync needed). DB0-17 (pins 6-23), DOTCLK (26), ENABLE (28), VSYNC (29), HSYNC (30) and\nRD (31) are all tied to GND per the datasheet's explicit 'fix low if not used' guidance\nfor the unused parallel-bus/RGB-interface pins -- not left floating. IM0 (36) is also\ntied GND and IM1/IM2 (37/38) to +3V3 for the 4-wire SPI mode strap. VCC (3) and VCI (39)\nboth go to +3V3 (digital I/O and analog display power rails, both 3.3V per the\ndatasheet). This sheet's own +3V3/GND power symbols don't drive those nets --\npower.kicad_sch does -- same convention as every other populated child sheet in this\nproject (see their own notes for why a per-sheet power_pin_not_driven ERC result on\nstandalone single-sheet checks is expected and not a real defect)." (at 20 300 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid b643acd0-f8ee-43e6-be49-3f6c609cbf5d)
  )
  (text "Connector: J501 is the LCSC FC-05B40P21H20 (C23398824, BXCONN), 40-position, 0.5mm\npitch, dual-contact (top-and-bottom entry, 'no polarity'), Flip-Top SMT FPC/ZIF\nconnector -- swapped in by pilink-4b6 (REQUIRED pre-fab fix) from the originally-\nspecified bottom-contact-only AFC01-S40FCA-00 (C262674, Jushuo), which does not\ncorrectly mate the display FPC's J-fold geometry (pilink-7el.12) under this project's\nback-face contact-side working assumption -- see\n.research/findings/2026-11-15-display-fpc-contact-side.md. The dual-contact part mates\neither orientation, removing the dependency on resolving contact side at all, with no\nchange to the proven J-fold geometry. Confirmed 2,635 units live LCSC stock at swap\ntime (2026-11-16) via the jlcpcb-search MCP tool; pitch/position-count/contact-type/\nlocking-feature all confirmed from its own LCSC spec table and independently\nre-derived from its own CAD drawing (BXCONN dwg BX-CN-001-A), recovered in this\nenvironment by hand-decompressing the datasheet PDF's content stream and replaying its\nvector path/bezier operators (no PDF rasterizer installed here). No stock KiCad symbol\nor footprint exists for this exact part, so both were hand-authored/reused for this\nbead (pico_link_custom:CFAF240320A0_FPC40 in symbols/pico_link_custom.kicad_sym;\nConnector_FPC:FC-05B40P21H20 in footprints/Connector_FPC.pretty/, registered in\nfp-lib-table under the existing Connector_FPC entry). The symbol's single-column pin\nlayout is a schematic drawing convenience, not a physical pinout diagram. PIN-1 --\nRESOLVED (pilink-4b6 fix round, 2026-11-16): independently confirmed via the\nEasyEDA/JLCPCB assembly-library footprint data for both parts\n(easyeda.com/api/products/<LCSC>/components -- answers a plain curl GET with no WAF\nblock, unlike the easyeda.com website itself) that the two parts number pin 1 from\nOPPOSITE physical ends: C23398824's own JLC footprint has pad 1 (and its silkscreen\ndot) at its RIGHT end; C262674's has pad 1 at its LEFT end, both in the same canonical\norientation (signal-pad row at the front edge, mounting tabs/body behind) -- agreeing\nwith the BXCONN drawing's own NO.1 marker (right end in its view 1). Because ZIF\ncontacts are straight-through, each PHYSICAL pad position keeps the SAME net it always\nhad; only the pad/pin NUMBER labels needed correcting. Fix applied: the footprint's\npads 1-40 were mirror-renumbered (physical position x=+9.75 is now pad '1', matching\nthe real part; was mislabeled '40') and the symbol's pins were mirror-renumbered in\nlockstep (pin k -> 41-k) so every signal (DB17-0, SDA, DOTCLK, HSYNC/VSYNC, RD/WR, RS,\nCS, RESET, IMx, power/ground) still lands on the same physical pad position as before\n-- verified via an exported-netlist diff showing J501's physical pin-to-net mapping is\nunchanged from the pre-fix state. CABLE-ENTRY-SIDE CAVEAT (still open, separate from\npin-1): whether the two parts' FPC cables insert from the same side relative to the\npad row could not be confirmed from the EasyEDA footprint data, LCSC product photos,\nor JLC parametric fields (both parts show identical 'Flip-Top'/'Right Angle' fields,\nno explicit entry-side attribute, and the old part's datasheet has no dimensioned\ndrawing to check against) -- flag for a human with physical samples before fab. The\nfootprint's pitch/span (0.5mm, 19.5mm pin1-pin40) are sourced from its own CAD drawing\nand cross-checked against the EasyEDA data; its mounting-pad (MP1/MP2) size/offset and\nsignal-pad length were corrected the same way (1.5mm wide x 2.5mm tall tabs centered\nat X=+/-11.45mm, 3.10mm from the signal pad row; 1.5mm-long signal pads) -- replacing\nplaceholder values reused from the prior AFC01 footprint. Its body/courtyard Y-profile\nis still an unmeasured placeholder from that prior footprint -- flag for a human\nKiCad-GUI pass before PCB fab, same caveat class this project already applies to the\nRP2350 QFN-80 and PSRAM USON-8 hand-authored footprints." (at 20 360 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid d3d3d5c7-bb11-4ca6-94fd-526311d57df6)
  )
  (text "GPIO assignment: GPIO29 (SPI1 CSn), GPIO30 (SPI1 SCK/RS), GPIO31 (SPI1 TX/MOSI/SDA),\nGPIO32 (D-C/WR), GPIO33 (RESET), GPIO34 (backlight CTRL/enable) -- picked from the generic bidirectional\nGPIO pool rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch exposes as global labels for every RP2350B GPIO not\nalready committed elsewhere. Confirmed free by grepping all of hardware/*.kicad_sch for\nevery GPIOx global label before picking (2026-11-15): input.kicad_sch claims only\nGPIO22-28 (A/B/X/Y + the volume encoder's 3 signals, per the two 2026-11-15 rotary-\nencoder ADRs); esp32_bt.kicad_sch uses named ESP32_* global labels, not GPIOx, and its\nRP2350-side GPIO mapping is still an open item on rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch (not this\nsheet's concern); usb_c.kicad_sch is still an empty skeleton. GPIO29-34 were untouched\nby all of the above. Each GPIOx label keeps the generic pool name as its real net\nidentity (required for it to actually join the same-named label on\nrp2350b_memory.kicad_sch) with a plain, non-connected text caption underneath for the\nlogical function name -- same convention input.kicad_sch uses for A/B/X/Y/VOL_*, and\nfor the same reason: a second schematic label on the same net would trip ERC's\nmultiple_net_names check." (at 20 425 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid b8f19b3b-6bc9-4ba1-b5e8-7c0742da8ef3)
  )
  (text "Backlight driver: the panel's LED_A/LED_K backlight string needs ~9V (VF 8.1-9.9V typ\n9.0V) at 40mA per the datasheet's section 11.1 -- not achievable from the 3.3V/5V rails\ndirectly. This was originally Diodes AP3036BKTR-G1 (LCSC C526368), copied directly from\nCrystalfontz's own 'LED Backlight Reference Schematic' (datasheet section 11.2), but\nAP3036BKTR-G1 was found to be at 0 stock (confirmed twice independently, see pilink-av8)\nwith no restock date, so U501 is now Diodes AP3031KTR-G1 (LCSC C82636, 11,130 units in\nstock, re-confirmed live via jlcpcb-search MCP 2026-11-15) -- same SOT-23-6 package, same\nboost topology and 200mV FB reference, but NOT pin-compatible: pin1=SW, pin2=GND, pin3=FB,\npin4=CTRL, pin5=OV, pin6=VIN, per the real AP3031 datasheet's own Pin Description table\n(independently re-extracted for pilink-av8 via a local zlib-inflate+regex PDF text\nextractor, no poppler/pypdf available in this sandbox). Three circuit differences from\nthe old AP3036B layout, all applied here:\n(1) AP3031 has no internal Schottky/VOUT pin -- pin1 (SW) datasheet text 'Connect\nexternal inductor and Schottky' requires the new external diode D501 (SW to VOUT, see\nits own note below) that AP3036B's circuit didn't need.\n(2) AP3031 adds pin5 OV (Over-voltage Protection Input, datasheet: 'Connect to the\noutput directly'). This symbol places OV at the exact pin slot/wire the old VOUT pin\noccupied, so OV is already on the VOUT net (shared with C502, LED_A and D501's cathode)\nwithout needing a separate drawn wire -- same electrical connection the bead asked for,\njust inherited from the existing node rather than a new wire segment.\n(3) L501 is 4.7uH (was 22uH) and C502 is 0.47uF (was 1uF), per the AP3031 datasheet's own\n'Typical Application' circuit (Figure 24, 3*13 WLEDs for an LCD backlight, 1MHz\nswitching) -- not AP3036B's values, which were tuned for a different IC. C501 (10uF VIN\nbypass) already matched that same reference circuit's C_IN and needed no change.\nR501 (FB-GND) stays 5.1R unchanged -- AP3031's FB reference is 200mV, identical to\nAP3036B's, so ILED = VFB/RFB = 200mV/5.1R ~= 39.2mA still matches the panel's 40mA spec\nexactly. VIN comes from this project's +3V3 rail (within AP3031's 2.7-16V input range,\nsame margin as before). CTRL goes to GPIO34 -- tied high enables the driver; firmware may\ninstead PWM this same pin for brightness dimming per AP3031's 'High Frequency Dimming\nControl' feature (same behavior AP3036B's CTRL had). Both are valid with this circuit;\nwhich one firmware uses is out of scope for this schematic.\n\nSourcing history: AP3036BKTR-G1 (LCSC C526368) was re-checked live via jlcpcb-search MCP\non 2026-11-15 and found still at 0 units in stock, same as pilink-7el.5's and pilink-av8's\nown investigation comments. The bead-named fallback, AW9364DNR (LCSC C401007), was\nindependently checked against its own datasheet and rejected: it is Awinic's '4-Channel\n1-wire Dimming LED Driver', a linear constant-current LED *sink* (VIN 2.8V-5.5V, no\ninductor, no boost stage), architecturally unable to produce this backlight's required\n~9V output from a 3.3V input -- an architecture mismatch, not just a pinout difference.\nAP3031KTR-G1 is a genuine topology-equivalent, in-stock substitute, verified against its\nown real datasheet text (not assumed from the part number alone) -- see pilink-av8 for\nthe full investigation and sourcing detail.\n\nFootprint correction (pilink-2wq): L501's footprint was Inductor_SMD:L_1210_3225Metric\n(EIA 1210, 3.2x2.5mm) -- a placeholder from before the actual part was picked. The part\nthis project's BOM selected for the 4.7uH/1.7A-Isat requirement, Cenker CKCS4018-4.7uH/M\n(LCSC C354574), is a 4.0x4.0x1.8mm part with its own purpose-built KiCad footprint\n(Inductor_SMD:L_Cenker_CKCS4018, confirmed present in this machine's stock footprint\nlibrary and datasheet-matched via its own .kicad_mod descr field) -- now corrected to\nmatch. Note this part is physically LARGER than the old 1210 placeholder, not smaller as\nan earlier BOM draft stated; PCB layout (pilink-7el.9) should allocate footprint area\naccordingly." (at 20 475 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid d580fa24-c63c-44b2-a59d-ee9cf513e297)
  )
)
